    "title": {
      "en": "\"Hiding the Wires\" Helps Usher in Web3's Killer App",
      "zh": "「藏起線路」將助推 web3 殺手級應用的誕生"
    },
    "author": "Chris Lyons",
    "summary": {
      "en": "Blockchains' technical superpowers make them special but have also hindered mainstream adoption, as insider jargon like \"NFTs\" and \"zkRollups\" and complex design deter the very creators and fans who benefit most. Mass adoption of consumer technology typically follows a pattern where an iconic company abstracts away the complexity to unlock a breakthrough app, just as email hid SMTP behind \"send\" and Spotify delivered playlists rather than file formats. In 2025, the industry will embrace the ethos of \"hiding the wires,\" designing simply and communicating clearly so that successful products solve problems instead of explaining them.",
      "zh": "區塊鏈的技術超能力使其與眾不同,卻也阻礙了主流採用——「NFT」「zkRollup」之類的圈內術語與複雜的設計,讓最能從中受益的創作者與粉絲望而卻步。消費科技的大規模普及通常遵循同一模式:某個指標性公司把複雜性抽象掉,進而催生出突破性應用,就像電子郵件把 SMTP 協定藏在「傳送」按鈕之後,Spotify 端出的是歌單而非檔案格式。預計 2025 年產業會擁抱「藏起線路」的精神,設計從簡、溝通清晰,讓成功的產品專注於解決問題,而不是解釋自己。"
    },
    "tags": [
      "ux",
      "adoption",
      "consumer",
      "abstraction"
    ],
    "source": "https://a16z.com/big-ideas-in-tech-2025/"
