    "title": {
      "en": "Countries Explore Putting Government Bonds Onchain",
      "zh": "各國探索將政府公債上鏈"
    },
    "author": "Brian Quintenz",
    "summary": {
      "en": "Putting government bonds onchain would create a government-backed, interest-bearing digital asset without the surveillance concerns of a CBDC, and could unlock new collateral demand in DeFi lending and derivatives protocols. As pro-innovation governments explore public, permissionless blockchains, some countries may trial issuing government bonds onchain; the UK is already exploring digital securities through an FCA sandbox. In the U.S., upcoming SEC treasury-clearing requirements will likely spur more conversations about how blockchains can improve transparency, efficiency, and participation in bond trading.",
      "zh": "將政府公債上鏈,可創造出一種由政府背書、附息的數位資產,同時避開央行數位貨幣(CBDC)的監控疑慮,並能為 DeFi(去中心化金融)借貸與衍生品協定釋放新的擔保品需求。隨著支持創新的各國政府持續探索公開、無需許可的區塊鏈,部分國家可能會試行在鏈上發行政府公債;例如英國已透過金融行為監理局(FCA)的沙盒探索數位證券。在美國,證管會(SEC)即將要求公債清算的新規,料將激起更多關於區塊鏈如何提升公債交易透明度、效率與參與度的討論。"
    },
