    "category": "crypto",
    "title": {
      "en": "The Crypto Industry Finally Gets Its Own App Stores, and Discovery",
      "zh": "加密產業終於有了自己的應用商店與發現機制"
    },
    "author": "Maggie Hsu",
    "summary": {
      "en": "When centralized platforms like Apple's App Store or Google Play block crypto apps, they limit top-of-funnel user acquisition, but new app stores and marketplaces are now providing ungated distribution and discovery. Examples include Worldcoin's World App marketplace, which onboarded hundreds of thousands of users to apps within days, and Solana's fee-free dApp Store, both showing how hardware as well as software may be a key advantage. Porting existing distribution from messaging or web2 apps remains hard, but more of this may happen in 2025.",
      "zh": "當蘋果 App Store 或 Google Play 等中心化平台封鎖加密應用時,便限縮了其漏斗頂端的使用者獲取;但如今新興的應用商店與市集正提供不設關卡的散布與發現管道。例子包括 Worldcoin 的 World App 市集——它在短短數天內為多款應用帶來數十萬使用者——以及 Solana 免手續費的 dApp Store;兩者都顯示出,硬體(而不只是軟體),可能正是加密應用商店的關鍵優勢。將通訊或 web2 應用的既有散布管道移植上鏈仍屬不易,但 2025 年可能會看到更多此類嘗試。"
    },
